abstract: >-
  The Digital Reference Material Document (DRMD) is an XML format for the documents that
  accompany reference materials: the RM certificate of a certified reference material and the
  product information sheet of any other reference material. Version 1.0.0 consists of an XML
  Schema (drmd.xsd), which defines the structure shared by both document types, and Schematron
  business rules (drmd-business-rules.sch), which check the requirements of ISO 33401:2024,
  Table 1, for each document type with four severity levels derived from the requirement levels
  of the standard. Values, units and uncertainties are written in the Digital System of Units
  (D-SI) of PTB, and shared building blocks are taken from the Digital Calibration Certificate
  (DCC) of PTB. The repository includes the vendored third-party schemas, an XML catalog for
  offline validation, two worked examples, a validation tool and a test that every rule fires.
keywords:
  - reference materials
  - certified reference materials
  - ISO 33401
  - digital certificate
  - XML Schema
  - Schematron
  - D-SI
  - DCC
  - metrology
  - quality infrastructure
